From 0ed63f725bedbea8bfd9ad7a6acd3b5490480323 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:04:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] shared: isValidMacAddress() refuses any character but hex
 digits and separators

At the 102.10 rebase (merge stop 63) Reaper's reaper_mac_or_empty() - a character
whitelist in front of isValidMacAddress() - gave way to upstream's isValidMacAddress()
alone on the AiMesh cfg-event paths (onboarding / cfg_onboarding.cgi, ob_selection,
config_changed, prefer_node_apply; upstream's remove_slave / reset_default /
device_reboot gates too). Upstream's function sets s = -1 on a foreign character and
carries on, so a separator after one hex digit (i / 2 - 1 == -1) resets the count:
A":A:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF and 0}],"k":[{"q":0:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF pass, and their quotes and
braces reach the JSON events httpd writes for cfg_server. The function now returns 0
on the first such character, which covers every caller; a real MAC never held one
(a stray character already failed unless a separator followed it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/httpd/web.c   | 7 +++----
 release/src/router/shared/misc.c | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/httpd/web.c b/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
index d4ef50f3200..ef82c3a9810 100644
--- a/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
+++ b/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
@@ -13425,10 +13425,9 @@ prepare_restore(webs_t wp){
 }
 
 /* reaper 2026-10-23: AiMesh re_mac / new_re_mac / target_bssid are printed unescaped into JSON events
-   for the closed cfg_server. Accept a MAC (isValidMacAddress: 12 hex digits, optional : or -) or an
-   empty value - stock passes empty values through and an empty string carries no quote or brace.
-   The character whitelist comes first so that, whatever isValidMacAddress() tolerates, nothing but
-   hex digits and separators can ever reach the event text. */
+   for the closed cfg_server. Since the 102.10 rebase the gates are upstream's isValidMacAddress();
+   shared/misc.c makes it refuse any character but hex digits and separators, so nothing else can
+   reach the event text. */
 #ifdef RTCONFIG_BHCOST_OPT
 /**
  * @brief Generate amas_wlcX_target_bssid nvram string to RE.
diff --git a/release/src/router/shared/misc.c b/release/src/router/shared/misc.c
index 9a783c90786..eb7c83f348f 100644
--- a/release/src/router/shared/misc.c
+++ b/release/src/router/shared/misc.c
@@ -6119,7 +6119,11 @@ int isValidMacAddress(const char* mac) {
 			++s;
 		}
 		else
-			s = -1;
+			/* Reaper 2026-10-27: any other character makes it no MAC. Stock set s = -1 and went
+			 * on, so a separator after one hex digit (i / 2 - 1 == -1) put the count back and
+			 * A":A:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF passed - a quote or brace into the JSON events httpd writes
+			 * for cfg_server from re_mac / new_re_mac / target_bssid. */
+			return 0;
 		++mac;
 	}
 	return (i == 12 && (s == 5 || s == 0));
-- 
